    <article class="prose article-body">
      <div class="note-box"><strong>Important disclaimer:</strong> This guide is for entertainment, journaling and self-reflection only. It is not medical, legal, financial, psychological or life-decision advice.</div>
      
<p class="lead">Astrology and numerology are both symbolic self-reflection systems, but they use different inputs. Astrology uses dates, signs and sometimes time and location. Numerology uses numbers from birth dates and names.</p>
<h2>Main differences</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Input</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Astrology</td><td>Birth date, signs, sometimes time and place</td><td>Personality themes, timing, relationship style</td></tr><tr><td>Numerology</td><td>Birth date and name letters</td><td>Life themes, expression style, simple journaling prompts</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2>Which should you use?</h2><p>If you like symbolic stories and relationship language, start with astrology. If you prefer simple calculations and number themes, start with numerology. Many people use both lightly.</p><div class="ad-slot">Advertisement space after AdSense approval</div>
<h2>Healthy approach</h2><p>Neither system should replace professional advice or personal judgment. Use them for curiosity, not certainty.</p>

